Z||000005||FieroJoe||03-10-2001||08:44 PM||||Happens to me too!  Especially this winter.  I have seen two 3 different fieros throughout the whole summer while I was driving mine.  A white wingless GT (saw him twice going the opposite direction on the highway in one week, we were both lookin at each other  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), a white SE, and another blue coupe!  That was the wierdest one, I was stunned.  Some lady was driving it and she gave me a smile and I waved.<P>But this winter, while mine is all torn apart and sitting in the barn, I have seen quite a few.  I think 6 different ones.  kinda wierd too, it being winter and all.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroPerformance||03-10-2001||11:03 PM||||This tends to happen to me as well. My theory is that while driving the Fiero you tend to be having too much fun or going too fast to notice the other cars on the road. While driving a different car you are going through a Fiero "withdrawl" and are looking for them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>When I do see another Fiero while driving mine I usualy get a friendly wave.<P>BTW: I think that the fast backs might look a little better without the spoiler also. I think that if I had a fast back I would take off the spoiler.<P>-Charlie<BR>-----<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com <A HREF="http://www.fieroperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroperformance.com</A> ||||reg||12
